  "description": "Demolition of existing garage and the construction of a front porch including relocation of the side entrance door to the front, a part two storey part single storey side extension and a single storey rear extension",
  "development_type": "Other house holder developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of its design, bulk, mass, scale and siting, would appear incongruous and out of keeping with the prevailing character of the host dwelling, the terrace row and the distinctiveness and historic character of the Becontree Estate. The proposal would a dominant addition which would fail to appear subordinate to the original dwelling and would disrupt the planned form of the estate, whilst also resulting in a detrimental loss of the &#39;bookend&#39; features of the dwelling&nbsp;and the open aspect to the corner plot. It would thereby cause undue harm to the character and appearance of the area, including&nbsp;moderate&nbsp;harm to the non-designated heritage asset. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and historic distinctiveness:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policy HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
